	spec: 'scripts/install-service installs a Linux systemd user unit for the current writable Hal checkout, using the absolute Bun runtime and src/main.ts serve directly, explicit WorkingDirectory and HAL_HOME, and the invoking PATH for child tools. It supports --print for inspection; installation refuses to overwrite a differing existing unit. It never edits config, stops a host, enables or starts a service, installs dependencies, or grants linger. The unit restarts crashes and deliberate exit 100 without a nested ./run supervisor; systemctl stop remains stopped. README.md links SERVER.md, which documents initial setup, hostMode server to keep peers from taking over, deliberate migration from an interactive host, enabling and authorization-dependent linger, logs, stop/restart and live-code updates, local/remote login and loopback TLS reverse-proxy security, and a NixOS declarative system service using an external writable checkout rather than an immutable package. Examples contain reserved domains and generic paths, not host-specific setup.',
